      "id": "p29",
      "title": "Idghām of Two Letters",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Two same letters: the first is sakin and merges into the second. Say it once with a shadda.\nMithlain (م ن): the first letter merges into the same letter, with ghunna, 2 counts\nMithlain (د ل): say it once with a shadda; no qalqala on دۡ\nMithlain (ك ب): say it once with a shadda; no qalqala on بۡ"
    },
    {
      "id": "p30",
      "title": "Idghām of Two Letters",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Mutajanisain: two different letters from the same makhraj.\nMutajanisain (ذ←ظ, د←ت): same makhraj: the first letter merges fully into the second\nMutajanisain (ت←د, ت←ط): same makhraj: the first letter merges fully into the second\nMutajanisain (ث←ذ, ب←م): same makhraj: the first letter merges fully into the second"
    },
    {
      "id": "p31",
      "title": "Idghām of Two Letters",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "In نَخۡلُقكُّم the ق disappears fully: say كّ.\nMutajanisain, incomplete (ط←ت): the heavy sound of طۡ stays, and there's no qalqala\nMutaqaribain (ل←ر, ق←ك): letters with close makharij: the first merges fully into the second"
    }
  ],
